    "body": "fix on issue/3085-bore-fallback-band · PR #4104 https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/4104 · pinned by the_unmeasured_bore_band_accepts_the_current_pin, the_unmeasured_bore_band_checks_each_boundary, the_unmeasured_bore_band_rejects_the_old_mesh_readings · merges when reviewed.\n\nThe current pin is (4688, 4660, 1980), not the older triple in this issue. Commit 2407d9b09 records the measurements after PR #3802. The fallback keeps the previous small band widths. Exact platform pins and safety assertions do not change.\n\nThe selected quick gate passed: 5 tests passed, 2 stayed ignored. Strict focused clippy passed. Restoring the old band made all three new tests fail. This uses the unit-test acceptance alternative, not a fourth-platform measurement. The universal light lane was not run because its broad release build exceeds this test-only scope. No green CI result is claimed.\n\nThe contributor claim remains a comment because this account cannot change upstream labels or assignees. The PR is ready for review. The issue remains open until maintainer merge.",
